Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:06:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] SA-2: consolidate duplicate FeatureFlag module onto
 canonical core/feature-flags

- Delete modules/feature-flags/ (controller + module): a thin duplicate
  exposing one read-only, auth-broken endpoint (GET /feature-flags/definitions)
  that never received SA-1A's @SuperadminRoute() fix despite the handoff
  doc claiming it had. Functionally equivalent, correctly-guarded endpoint
  already exists at GET /flags/admin/all (core/feature-flags), confirmed
  via svc.getAllFlags() returning the same ALL_FLAGS catalog.

- app.module.ts: import FeatureFlagsModule directly from
  core/feature-flags/feature-flags.module instead of the deleted
  modules/feature-flags/feature-flags.module. Previously the core module
  was only alive transitively via CronEngineModule's own import -- an
  unintentional coupling between scheduling infra and the FeatureFlag API
  surface. Now explicitly registered at the application level.

- cron-engine.module.ts: unchanged. It already imports the canonical
  core/feature-flags/feature-flags.module (same class reference), so
  AppModule + CronEngineModule both importing it is a valid, deduped
  Nest dependency graph -- not a new duplicate.

Repo-wide grep confirmed before deletion: no other references to
modules/feature-flags, feature-flags.controller (modules/ variant), or
the '/feature-flags' route anywhere in backend/frontend/superadmin/mobile,
no e2e specs, no postman collection, no docs/ dir mentioning it.

Verification note: sandbox cannot run pnpm install / prisma generate /
full build (network-restricted, same limitation as prior sessions).
Server-side verification required before considering this fully landed:
see Phase C checklist in handoff notes.
